[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128294,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal nerve sheath myxoma is a benign peripheral nerve sheath tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128295,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9562/0 Dermal nerve sheath myxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128296,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F24 &amp; XH3L35 Benign cutaneous neoplasms of neural or nerve sheath origin &amp; Nerve sheath myxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128297,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> classic or myxoid variant of neurothekeoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128298,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128299,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal nerve sheath myxoma occurs in the distal extremities, particularly the fingers (36% of cases), toes, and lower extremities {16327434; 11070116}. It rarely involves the spinal canal {23306964}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128300,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours manifest as small, superficial, slow-growing asymptomatic masses; some are painful {16327434}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128301,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal nerve sheath myxomas are rare. The two largest modern series describe 68&nbsp;tumours arising over a wide age range (8&ndash;72&nbsp;years), with a peak in the mid-thirties and a slight male predominance {16327434; 11070116}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128302,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128303,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal nerve sheath myxoma was previously called &ldquo;classic or myxoid variant of neurothekeoma&rdquo; {7446487}. However, pathological {11070116; 17592278; 16327434; 17325474} and molecular data {21297585} demonstrated the Schwann cell derivation of dermal nerve sheath myxoma, which is clinically and biologically distinct from neurothekeoma. Thus, the gene signature of dermal nerve sheath myxomas is similar to that of dermal schwannomas, whereas cellular neurothekeomas more closely resemble cellular fibrous histiocytomas {21297585}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128304,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients typically present with rubbery/firm tumours in the dermis or subcutis, ranging from 4 to 45&nbsp;mm (most &lt;&nbsp;25&nbsp;mm). Cut section shows well-demarcated, glistening, white to translucent mucoid nodules {16327434}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128305,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal nerve sheath myxoma characteristically shows a multinodular growth pattern, abundant myxoid matrix, and a dense fibrous border in the dermis, subcutis, or both; it rarely extends to skeletal muscle. Neoplastic cells are small, epithelioid, ring-like, stellate, and spindled Schwann cells in cords, nests, and syncytial-like aggregates, with mild nuclear atypia. Some show ring-like morphology, resembling lipoblasts; rarely, multivacuolated cells with spider-like cytoplasmic processes, nuclear palisading, or Verocay body&ndash;like structures are seen. Scattered moderate pleomorphism, similar to that seen in ancient schwannomas, may be present. Mitoses are absent to very few {16327434}.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>S100 is diffusely positive, and GFAP and CD57 are also often positive {6365307; 2645040; 16327434; 11070116}. Rare cells are positive for AE1/AE3, and the fibrous capsule may show scattered EMA-positive cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128306,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128307,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128308,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a small, superficial tumour in a distal extremity (especially the fingers); a multilobular, myxoid neoplasm with S100-positive bland spindled and epithelioid cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128309,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128310,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 284,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal nerve sheath myxomas are benign tumours with high rates of local recurrence, particularly in the fingers. In the largest modern study, local recurrences occurred in 47% of patients, nearly one&nbsp;third experienced two to five local recurrences, and 25% of patients had active disease at last follow-up {16327434}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:49:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]